From 91f87bed9bc42cc97630f4a66ed91d3513bac3cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rasheed <arasheedu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:46:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] llm: forward llama-server trace events at layers/full
 detail

When a request is traced at layers/full detail, or in layer/sample step
mode, and the runner has the visualizer patch (probed once per runner with
POST /trace/ack: 409 patched, 404 stock), add the trace object to the
/completion and /v1/chat/completions requests and forward the __trace
events of every chunk through the request tracer:

- steps shifted from llama-server's 1-based to the tracer's 0-based count;
  one tracer step per generated token (predicted_n), so they line up
- t_ns rebased with the smallest receive-minus-__trace_t_ns offset seen
- events sorted by t_ns (prefill.batch is held back by llama-server)
- llama-server's prefill.batch/done and decode.sample replace the
  synthesized ones; decode.logits still comes from n_probs
- trace-only chunks (content "" or choices []) are forwarded at once and
  skip the token-repeat check; the chat final array's trailing chunks
  are drained for their events
- step-mode acks are posted to /trace/ack, and continue is sent when the
  request ends, the client goes away or the visualizer socket drops

Requests at basic detail, with tracing off or to a stock runner carry no
trace field.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
